====================================================================================================
WHY — LINK-PATH SUPPORT (coding, historical: the 312.8 -> 717.7 -> 220.0 swing)
====================================================================================================
GEKS sets a quarter's level as the mean over every populated path base->l->t.
MIN_MATCH deletes links, so it shrinks that mean's support. Collapse to one
link and the 'index' is a single bilateral.

  coding historical: 190 gigs, 21 quarters, base=2020Q1
  quarter pairs with <3 matched gigs: 12/210 (6%)

  MIN_MATCH=3: 2025Q1 = 312.8, supported by 8 link path(s); direct 2020Q1->2025Q1 bilateral: NO (1 matched gigs)
    link contributions (ln, high to low): 2022Q1=+1.97, 2024Q1=+1.31, 2020Q4=+1.23, 2021Q2=+1.09 ...

  MIN_MATCH=4: 2025Q1 = 717.7, supported by 1 link path(s); direct 2020Q1->2025Q1 bilateral: NO (1 matched gigs)
    link contributions (ln, high to low): 2022Q1=+1.97

  MIN_MATCH=5: 2024Q4 = 220.0, supported by 17 link path(s); direct 2020Q1->2024Q4 bilateral: NO (3 matched gigs)
    link contributions (ln, high to low): 2022Q1=+1.25, 2022Q2=+1.23, 2024Q1=+1.21, 2021Q4=+1.11 ...

  => at k=4 the terminal level rests on ONE link, and it is the most extreme
     of the eight available at k=3. The +129% jump is the estimator behaving
     as defined on a chain this thin, not a defect. Read it as: the historical
     coding level is NOT IDENTIFIED, which its +/-61% band does not convey.
